<article class="env-lemma" id="0532">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0532">Lemma <span data-tag="0532">15.21.4</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $S = R[T_1, \ldots , T_ n]/J$. Assume $J$ contains elements of the form $P_ i(T_ i)$ with $P_ i(T) = \prod _{j = 1, \ldots , d_ i} (T - \alpha _{ij})$ for some $\alpha _{ij} \in R$. For $\underline{k} = (k_1, \ldots , k_ n)$ with $1 \leq k_ i \leq d_ i$ consider the ring map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Phi _{\underline{k}} : R[T_1, \ldots , T_ n] \to R, \quad T_ i \longmapsto \alpha _{ik_ i}  \]
</div>
  <p> Set $J_{\underline{k}} = \Phi _{\underline{k}}(J)$. Then the image of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is equal to $V(\bigcap J_{\underline{k}})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This lemma proves itself. Hint: $V(\bigcap J_{\underline{k}}) = \bigcup V(J_{\underline{k}})$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>